{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-008", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Bangladesh growth seen at 3.4% in FY26 & FY27: World Bank", "content": "Bangladesh’s economy is projected to grow 3.4 per cent in FY26 and FY27, with exports losing momentum, investment softening and inflation keeping business costs high, according to the World Bank.\nGDP growth may improve to 3.9 per cent in FY28 if energy supply eases and reforms accelerate.\nRevenue was 8.3 per cent of GDP, the fiscal deficit widened to 3.9 per cent and bad loans reached 33.2 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-growth-seen-at-3-4-in-fy26-fy27-world-bank-314057-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-009", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "World Bank lifts Vietnam GDP forecast to 7.4%", "content": "World Bank has raised Vietnam’s 2026 GDP growth forecast to 7.4 per cent, the highest in East Asia and Pacific and 1.1 points above April.\nManufacturing and AI-related exports drive the outlook; AI goods made up over 70 per cent of Vietnam’s export growth by April 2026.\nVietnam has the region’s largest textile sector relative to GDP, but faces pressure from import growth and reserves.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/world-bank-lifts-vietnam-gdp-forecast-to-7-4--314045-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-010", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "PC and polyester yarn soften in Indian market; viscose holds steady", "content": "Polyester-cotton, polyester and speciality yarn prices fell in Ludhiana and Surat as weak demand and tight payments weighed on Indian markets.\nViscose yarn stayed steady in Mumbai and Surat amid muted purchases and uncertain weaving demand.\nNorth Indian cotton rose ₹40-50 (~$0.41-0.52) per maund in two days, tracking ICE cotton gains despite higher arrivals of 17,000 bales.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pc-and-polyester-yarn-soften-in-indian-market-viscose-holds-steady-314043-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-011", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s trade deficit widens 29% YoY in July-August FY27", "content": "Bangladesh's trade deficit widened 29 per cent to $3.82 billion in July-August FY27 as imports outpaced exports, Bangladesh Bank data showed.\nImports rose 12.1 per cent to $12.20 billion; exports grew 5.8 per cent to $8.38 billion and RMG exports rose 5.3 per cent to $7.49 billion.\nRemittances rose nearly 19 per cent to $5.83 billion, lifting the current account surplus to $599 million.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-trade-deficit-widens-29-yoy-in-july-august-fy27-314041-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-012", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton continues to rise on weaker dollar, physical demand", "content": "ICE cotton futures rose for a third session, with the December 2026 contract up 35 points at 81.21 cents per pound on weaker US dollar support, agricultural strength and lower-price demand.\nThe contract has gained 345 points in three sessions, but volume fell to 46,256 contracts and open interest dropped to 382,377.\nUS crop conditions slipped, while China's post-holiday reopening is awaited.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-continues-to-rise-on-weaker-dollar-physical-demand-314033-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-013", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline", "plunge"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "US splits $44 bn apparel market as China imports fall 31.5%", "content": "US HS61+62 apparel imports fell 8.3 per cent year on year to $44.06 billion in January-July 2026; China and India made up about 83 per cent of the net decline.\nChina plunged 31.5 per cent and India fell 25.3 per cent, while Vietnam, Cambodia and Indonesia strengthened positions.\nSection 301 duties began on July 24, so TexPro shows pre-tariff repositioning rather than a tariff-led shift.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-splits-44-bn-apparel-market-as-china-imports-fall-31-5--314044-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-014", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The next order: Will it go to Bangladesh?", "content": "Bangladesh apparel faces buyer diversification as retailers reassess sourcing exposure, country risks and post-LDC trade uncertainty.\nEU EBA access will remain for three years after graduation, but Vietnam already has an EU FTA and India is improving access.\nRecent gas shortages disrupted production and shipments, making durable energy supply and a longer-term EU trade deal critical.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/the-next-order-will-it-go-to-bangladesh--313992-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
